types.doc:
Builds Materia scene artifacts from MachineKit assemblies. Occurrences whose components share a
designation share one geometry part, so a scene definition may stand for several occurrences;
`shareDefinitions` keeps the connectors of all of them on it.

Complete fixed/floating SFU20 axis. Purchased parts use their catalogue geometry;
only base, rail risers, carriage and motor bracket are fabricated.
DSG depths (12/10 mm), 16 mm race root and 6 mm retaining-nut height are explicit reference assumptions.

Offset spindle-motor shelf support. Bottom foot lands on the tapered collar;
the upper bridge reaches the existing shelf. Origin at spindle X/Y, head top.
Nominal fabricated geometry; welds and fasteners are not qualified.

Assumed three-phase winding data. Torque constant uses phase RMS current;
back-EMF constant is line-to-line RMS volts per rad/s. They are stated separately.
Phase resistance is ohms, and mechanical efficiency excludes copper loss.

fields.doc:
Advance one tick. `loadWatts` is the measured demand at the pack bus;
`chargerWatts` is available output at the charger connector before pack
charge losses. Positive current in the resulting state means discharge.

types.doc:
Assumed three-phase rectifier with a capacitor bus and integrated regenerative shunt.
Line voltage is phase-to-phase RMS. The nominal unloaded bus is its peak;
this reference model does not simulate ripple or mains impedance.

An arc torch and the channels that work it, named `<prefix>/<member>.<signal>`:
- `channel`, digital: lights the arc (the `Arc` control);
- `wireSpeedChannel`, analog: the wire feed speed, in metres per minute;
- `voltageChannel`, analog: the voltage setpoint, in volts;
- `sensor`, a `tool_weld` frame: arc established, current (A), voltage (V), touch, fault code and the
mains power the supply draws (W), in that order.
`controlPort` is the inlet the channels drive through the feeder and the supply, and
`tcpConnector` is the wire tip.

CAD realization consumes the neutral plan. Loose screws/clamps are released first;
adhesive joints are released explicitly. Cores and supports participate in the
appropriate bed/fill withdrawal graph; EPS breakup remains a manual operation.

fields.doc:
The mission for the seams `found` in `weldment`, welded with the recipes for their legs in `wire`, the weld metal carried
by the occurrence `metal`, lengths in the scene's unit (`metresPerUnit` metres to one). `home` is where the torch starts;
`access`, when given, judges every seam.
